# Deploy-critical files must reach Linux with LF endings. A CRLF shebang makes
# the kernel look for the interpreter "/bin/sh\r", which fails as
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" -- the container then dies at
# startup with no useful error. Scoped deliberately to the files that run on
# Linux rather than a repo-wide `* text=auto`, which would renormalize the many
# Python sources that are already committed with CRLF (harmless: Python 3 reads
# CRLF source fine) and bury real changes in whitespace churn.
*.sh              text eol=lf
Dockerfile        text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*      text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml  text eol=lf
env.example       text eol=lf
*.env.example     text eol=lf
